WEBVTT

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.710
I'll see you later then.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:35.710
Bye!

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.940
Good morning!

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.350
Good morning. Are you
job hunting again today?

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.350
Yes...well...

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.080
It must be rough.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:52.380
Once I find a job, I'm sure Yagami
will give up and move back home.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.930
We can't leave things
the way they are.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.070
You're right.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:06.380
- Please do your best.
- I will! Goodbye.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.300
- Your tie is crooked.
- Thanks.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.640
Godai!

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.840
You forgot this.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.450
Here. Your handkerchief.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.050
How could you forget it after
I ironed it for you last night?

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.360
T-Thanks.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.810
- Hey, your tie is crooked.
- Forget it! It's not!

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.640
It is. C'mon, turn this way.
You're such a handful.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:33.930
Okay. Good to go.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:38.040
- I'm off then, Manager...
- Go! You're going to be late.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.800
Come home early, okay?

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.150
- Hey, the phone's ringing.
- All right.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:01.300
Sorry, dear, but can you get that?
I'm a little busy right now.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.180
I tell you...

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.330
Hello. Yagami residence.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.460
Ms. Kamiogi! Thank you for
looking after my daughter.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.770
Sorry to call so late.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.580
I know Ibuki hasn't been coming
to school because of illness

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.840
but I overheard a
disturbing rumor.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.490
Rumor?

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:33.260
Not only is she in good health,
but that she is living with a man!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.790
Hello?

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.830
- Hello?
- Yes?

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:46.860
I'm calling because I want to
ask Ibuki directly. Is she home?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.710
Yes...er...but she's in bed
since she's so ill.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.290
- Can't you hear her coughing?
- Huh?

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.090
Damn it! It's going around
as a rumor already!

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.960
You can't cover for her forever.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.270
So what should we do?

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.430
We have to get her back
before she's expelled.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.910
I know that!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.800
I do, but...

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:25.680
I'm not going home until you do
something about Godai's job!

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:30.610
Even I can't get Godai into
Mitsutomo Corporation already.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.110
What about another company?

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.110
Another company?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.320
And so, the man at the store
stared at me and said

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.670
"I'll give you a discount because
you look like a newlywed."

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.600
I guess I'll make some coffee.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.360
Oh, and I recycled the books
in the closet for some money.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.610
Hmm...Where did I put the sugar?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.370
- Can you be quiet?
- Huh?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.380
Oh, no. I broke it.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.940
Yahoo!

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.810
Aunty's here.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.610
Let's have a drink.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.050
Godai, I hear you hit the pavement
again today.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.130
Such hard work.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:22.000
Oh! Is that your resume?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.900
No matter how many you write,
it's hopeless.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:29.410
Yeah. He should give up.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:34.440
And I don't think keeping Ibuki
hostage is going to work on her dad.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.790
Stop making a fool of me!
I'm not counting on him.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.920
I'll do it on my own.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:47.100
Godai is just destined to
walk in the shadows of life.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:51.110
- Yeah!
- Poor kid.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.060
Anyway, forget about
finding a job. Let's drink!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.760
Yeah!

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:02.200
Enough is enough!
Get out! Now!

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:05.610
I'll never forgive anyone
who harasses Godai.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:15.010
What awful people, barging their
way in here night after night.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.550
What do they think
this room is anyway?

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.900
They lack manners.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:24.490
- Yagami, you know...
- I know.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.980
No matter what
I'm on your side'.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:32.760
If there's anything I can do,
tell me.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:38.240
Er...can you keep it down?

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:40.440
Okay!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:03.600
You know, you make me nervous
when you stare like that.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.370
- I'm sorry.
- As long as you get it.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.850
So this is what it feels like
to live a life of love.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:23.590
By staring at the back of
the one I love... somehow I...

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:27.590
I...

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.360
That should do it.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:44.180
She's cute when she's
quietly sleeping.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.410
- Dad...
- Huh?

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.010
Dad...

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.360
You dummy.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.940
I'll settle this once and for all
with her father tomorrow.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.180
Dear, I'm going to bed first.
Don't drink too much.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:39.190
It's not like I can't get him into one
of Mitsutomo's subsidiary companies...

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:53.410
And you call yourself
a father?

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.120
Your young daughter is
staying at a man's place

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:01.660
and you don't try to bring her home?
What about your parental obligations?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.500
I'm going to give him
a piece of my mind.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.370
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:15.630
I've long given up on
Mitsutomo Corporation anyway.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.870
I don't need to kiss
Yagami's Father's Feet.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.140
Hey, Godai.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:23.840
H-Hello.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.100
Sorry to keep you.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.250
No, I'm sorry for calling you
out during lunch.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:34.810
Er...

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.370
What is it you want
to tell me?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.020
Actually, Father...

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.890
It's premature to be
calling me "father"

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:11.620
Premature, my foot!
Anyway, I have a problem.

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:18.000
I know. It's not easy to find a job
with your college background.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.030
It's not about that. It's in
regards to your daughter.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.320
My daughter?

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:28.650
Don't you feel sorry for her?

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:33.330
And she's burdening me
by staying in my room.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:36.940
What? You're saying
my daughter's a burden?

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.310
Yes, to be honest.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.340
So you make her out to
be a burden

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:47.820
after you figured out you can't
use her to get a job?

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.220
- You lowlife!
- Give me a break!

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.660
I'm in love with Manager!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:55.970
What?

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.600
Are you ready to order?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.840
- Iced coffee, please.
- Thank you.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.790
Is what you said true?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:14.120
Yes, that's why it was never
my intention to use your daughter.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.780
Does Ibuki know how you feel?

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.870
She does. That's why she's
being so aggressive.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.540
I see.
So that's the story.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:28.180
Please come and get your daughter
as soon as possible.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:29.960
Excuse me.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:35.540
Why, that was easy.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:01.690
I can't honestly say that
I wasn't using Ibuki a little.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:07.020
But it's not right. I have to find
a job on my own.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:12.840
Maybe I'll stop by the college
job-find office tomorrow.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.420
- Godai, hurry!
- What's going on?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:28.010
There's a fire...
in your room!

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:28.850
What?

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.320
It's a fire! A fire!

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:33.090
Oh, no!

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.490
Fire? Where?

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.300
- Godai! Hurry!
- Coming!

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.320
Geez..!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.600
She's frying mackerel?

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.210
Whew!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.620
What's wrong, everyone?

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:09.660
Will the mackerel be
bitter or salty?

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:13.170
My room is filled
with smoke too.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.890
I'm just glad it wasn't a fire.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:17.170
Fire?

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:19.760
I get it now.

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.970
I'm sorry to cause a commotion.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:24.170
Sorry doesn't cut it!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:29.100
Don't you know what'll happen
if you fry mackerel without ventilation?

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:33.450
That was the last straw.
Get out!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:40.160
But... I only wanted you to
enjoy some seasonal mackerel,

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:45.260
yet you're kicking me out.
What cruel words.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.540
I-I must not give in
to those eyes!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:53.130
Anyway, go home today.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.050
Hello?

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:58.870
Hello!

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.270
Is anyone home?

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:09.430
You know I can't go home.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:14.480
Don't worry. I met with your dad
today and settled everything.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:16.490
With my dad?

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.590
He's waiting for you at home.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:24.970
- What about your job?
- Did you settle that too?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.770
I see...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:31.270
You agreed to give back his daughter
in exchange for a job.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.340
You go, Godai!

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:40.520
Give me a break! You think I want
to be indebted to that stubborn man?

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.960
I want to find a job
on my own.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.830
That's right. Godai is pounding
the pavement every day.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.360
Although he gets rejected
everywhere he goes.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.910
- Hello.
- Dad!

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.340
I know I'm interrupting,
but I came in anyway.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.230
Thank you for today.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:07.580
No!

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.130
No. I'm not going home.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.470
- Godai...
- Yes?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.090
Take this without a word.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:20.590
Huh?

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:23.620
It's a letter of recommendation
for a subsidiary company.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.490
Letter of recommendation?

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:29.090
This will get you in for sure.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.070
But I...

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:36.330
We've had many misunderstandings.
This is a token of my regret.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.680
Please accept it.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:42.180
Come now, Ibuki.
Let's go home.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.770
If you don't come home,
I'll take back the letter.

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:48.790
What?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:53.220
Godai's future is hinging on you.
What's your decision?

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.570
Sorry to barge in
so late at night.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.360
Not at all.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.410
Thank you for everything.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.940
Godai, can I talk to you?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.980
What?

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:22.920
Don't forget that you got a job
because I'm moving home.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.980
- Good night!
- Ibuki!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.830
Dad! Hurry!

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.620
Excuse us.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.600
What a ruckus that was.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.430
But at least Godai got
a guaranteed job.

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.500
That means...

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:44.680
Let's drink! We have
reason to pre-celebrate!

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:45.440
Yeah!

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.510
- You too, Kyoko.
- Coming.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.100
We're pre-celebrating.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:12.870
Let's join them!

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.450
You got a tentative offer
for a job?

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:35.460
It's for a small computer company
called Katsugi Inc.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.190
Never heard of it.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:40.750
It's rapidly grown these past
two or three years.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.940
I hear companies like that
are pretty unstable.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:45.940
Hey...

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:52.070
But I never thought you'd be the first
in our class to land a possible position.

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.610
It's because of ability.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:54.970
Yeah, right.

00:17:56.480 --> 00:18:00.570
You better get on the ball or
you'll miss the job boat too.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.630
I can just repeat another year
of school if worse comes to worst.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.460
I don't have reason to rush
like you.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:10.660
Are both of you going to work
after you get married?

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.930
I want to be the breadwinner
if possible.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.970
Don't be naive. Once you finish school,
your stipend stops.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.730
And because it's a small company,
you won't get paid much.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.070
You'll barely be able
to support yourself.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:29.080
How can you be so pessimistic?

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:32.810
- Are there any bright spots?
- Sure, there are.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:40.320
I'm sure Manager can
withstand poverty.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:53.250
Do you really think women
like to be poor?

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.370
I didn't say she'll like it.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:02.710
It's just that she's humble,
and she seems quite frugal.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.160
We can rent a six-mat room
for starters.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:13.510
I'm sorry, Kyoko.
I don't bring home enough.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.690
Not at all. I like living
the simple life.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:21.050
And because the room is small
I can be close to you always.

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:23.430
Thanks, Kyoko.

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:26.330
You're so understanding.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:30.030
Kyoko...

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.850
Your brain must be
rose-colored.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:45.930
Manager, are the rumors true about
Hiyori Corporation being in danger?

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:49.520
Well, if there is a domino
effect with bankruptcies,

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:53.290
the companies within our enterprise
will sustain damage,

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.710
- so I did what I could but...
- It was no use?

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.530
At this point, we have no choice
but to cut them off.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.390
- Is there something wrong?
- Something is nagging at me...

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.070
What could it be?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:18.240
Oh, well. If I can't remember
it probably wasn't important.

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:23.050
I shouldn't stress out
over everything.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.170
Want to have a drink tonight?

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:27.960
Sure.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:37.440
- Welcome back.
- I'm home.

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:41.010
- Did your paperwork go okay?
- Yes, thank you.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.500
Er...here.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:47.810
It's something small to congratulate
you on finding employment.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:53.390
Thank you for thinking about me.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.660
May I open it?

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.130
Sure. It's really nothing.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.860
What could it be?
I'm so happy.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:05.140
Wow! A necktie!

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:09.470
I thought you could never have
enough of them after you find a job.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.300
It's nice.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.910
With this on, I feel I can
tackle anything.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:19.220
That's not true.

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:24.240
I don't mean that you
can't tackle anything.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:31.050
Watch me, Kyoko.
I'm going to work hard.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.490
Yes, rather than working
for a big, impersonal company...

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:39.170
Yes, I'll probably get more
responsibilities at a small company.

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:42.950
And it's easier to take things
on at a small company.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:47.800
Y-Yes. I'll get you something
when I get my first paycheck.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:52.480
You don't have to. I know
you won't be getting paid much...

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:53.810
I mean...

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.860
- W-Well, excuse me...
- Sure.

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:10.050
It doesn't seem like she has
high hopes for me.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:16.870
- Hey, company employee.
- Why are you looking so glum?

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:18.330
Are we drinking again?

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:22.210
Of course. This is to celebrate
you finding a job.

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:25.220
I'm going to party hearty tonight!

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:28.240
You always party hearty anyway.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.850
- C'mon. Grab a glass.
- All right.

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:34.390
Rather, hurry and get
to Manager's office.

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:41.160
I think she was hard at work
cooking for tonight's celebration.

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:44.170
- She looked so happy.
- What?!

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:46.670
Come in.

00:22:49.310 --> 00:22:50.290
Kyoko...

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:54.370
Perfect timing!
Help me carry this.

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:00.930
Wow! What a spread!
Let me have a taste.

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:01.620
Hey.

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:05.630
Sorry, but can you turn
the TV off?

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:06.420
Sure.

00:23:06.490 --> 00:23:13.200
Next in the news, Hiyori Corp, a rapidly
growing software company, has folded.

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:15.470
Other companies
connected to Hiyori,

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:19.900
including Isan Electronics,
Karui Company and Katsugi Inc.,

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:22.560
have also gone bankrupt
in a chain reaction.

00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:24.910
This concludes today's news.

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:30.950
Didn't they just mention Katsugi Inc.
on the news? Godai!

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.800
What? Asuna?

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.460
Lovesick?

00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:50.530
She can't get out of bed.

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:54.350
You don't have time to be
gossiping about other people, Godai.

00:23:54.430 --> 00:23:56.620
Oh, no! Yagami!

00:23:56.710 --> 00:24:00.690
Next: "One-Track Love!
Yagami and Asuna Never Say Die"

00:24:00.780 --> 00:24:02.630
I ran away from home again!
